        "item": [
          {
            "lang": "en",
            "text": "<p>There are about 40 species of cats in the world, and they occur naturally on every continent except Antarctica and Oceania, where cats arrived only with human settlers. All of them descend from a common ancestor that lived some 10 million years ago, and for this reason they share the same body plan, with retractable claws, teeth shaped to slice meat, sharp night vision and a build suited to the ambush. A lion of 190 kg and a house cat of 4 kg are, in this sense, variations on a single theme.</p>\n\n<p>This course follows that group in sections organized by size and by the relationship each group has with people. The species and breeds listed below are examples, chosen to show the diversity within each group, and each group includes many others.</p>\n\n<table style=\"width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;margin-top:16px\">\n  <tbody>\n    <tr>\n      <td style=\"width:140px;padding:12px;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;vertical-align:middle\">\n<img src=\"https://edukors.org/content/cats_world/cats%20full%20LION.png\" alt=\"Big cat (lion)\" title=\"Big cat (lion)\" style=\"width:110px;height:auto;display:block;margin:auto;cursor:zoom-in\" onclick=\"var o=document.createElement('div');o.style.cssText='position:fixed;inset:0;background:rgba(0,0,0,.85);display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;z-index:9999;cursor:zoom-out;padding:16px';var i=document.createElement('img');i.src=this.src;i.alt=this.alt;i.style.cssText='max-width:95vw;max-height:95vh;object-fit:contain;border-radius:6px;box-shadow:0 4px 24px rgba(0,0,0,.5)';o.appendChild(i);o.onclick=function(){o.remove()};document.body.appendChild(o);\">\n      </td>\n      <td style=\"padding:12px;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;vertical-align:middle\"><strong>Big cats</strong>, such as the lion, tiger, jaguar, leopard, cougar and cheetah.</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td style=\"width:140px;padding:12px;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;vertical-align:middle\">\n<img src=\"https://edukors.org/content/cats_world/cats%20full%20LYNX.png\" alt=\"Small wild cat (lynx)\" title=\"Small wild cat (lynx)\" style=\"width:110px;height:auto;display:block;margin:auto;cursor:zoom-in\" onclick=\"var o=document.createElement('div');o.style.cssText='position:fixed;inset:0;background:rgba(0,0,0,.85);display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;z-index:9999;cursor:zoom-out;padding:16px';var i=document.createElement('img');i.src=this.src;i.alt=this.alt;i.style.cssText='max-width:95vw;max-height:95vh;object-fit:contain;border-radius:6px;box-shadow:0 4px 24px rgba(0,0,0,.5)';o.appendChild(i);o.onclick=function(){o.remove()};document.body.appendChild(o);\">\n      </td>\n      <td style=\"padding:12px;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;vertical-align:middle\"><strong>Small wild cats</strong>, such as the Eurasian lynx, serval, caracal and ocelot.</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td style=\"width:140px;padding:12px;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;vertical-align:middle\">\n<img src=\"https://edukors.org/content/cats_world/cats%20full%20CAT.png\" alt=\"Domestic cat\" title=\"Domestic cat\" style=\"width:110px;height:auto;display:block;margin:auto;cursor:zoom-in\" onclick=\"var o=document.createElement('div');o.style.cssText='position:fixed;inset:0;background:rgba(0,0,0,.85);display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;z-index:9999;cursor:zoom-out;padding:16px';var i=document.createElement('img');i.src=this.src;i.alt=this.alt;i.style.cssText='max-width:95vw;max-height:95vh;object-fit:contain;border-radius:6px;box-shadow:0 4px 24px rgba(0,0,0,.5)';o.appendChild(i);o.onclick=function(){o.remove()};document.body.appendChild(o);\">\n      </td>\n      <td style=\"padding:12px;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;vertical-align:middle\"><strong>Domestic cats</strong>, with breeds such as the Siamese, Persian, Turkish Angora and Bengal.</td>\n    </tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>"
          }
        ]
